This program is an independent command-line prompt optimizer.
It does not contain source code or meta-prompt text from the project below.

Credit
------
Architecture and product idea credited to:

  prompt-optimizer
  Copyright (C) 2025 linshenkx
  https://github.com/linshenkx/prompt-optimizer
  License: GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only

What was not copied: packages/core, default-templates, UI, storage,
history, or any other file from that repository.

What this program implements on its own: an intake analyst that writes
a JSON brief (mode, strategy, assumptions, expert practices,
placeholders, questions), automatic mode routing (system, user, image),
up-front interactive questions, domain craft references, fenced
interpolation, iterate-by-pipe, a scored draft → critique → revise loop
with best-of selection, and a Magpie OpenAI-compatible client
defaulting to grok/grok-4.7. The loop matches the upstream product sequence
(optimize, then an evaluation, then iterate with that evaluation as
the change request). The prompt text is not theirs.

